# a `*.ext` line skips that whole file type everywhere - any directory whose
# only entrypoint is that type is left alone (no wine/mono wrapper, no link),
# so new tools of that type are covered automatically without listing dirs.
#
# `*.exe` is OFF here, so Windows tools are callable by name: run through
# mono (.NET) or wine when installed, otherwise linked onto PATH as-is so
# `nc64.exe` / `which procdump64.exe` find the file (for transferring to a
# target). Uncomment the next line to keep every .exe copy-only instead:
# *.exe
